==============================================================================
A. ZETA POSITIVE CONTROL -- symbol of f_k(x) = (1/k)floor(1/x) - floor(1/(kx))
==============================================================================
  Structural fact used (exact, elementary): f_k is CONSTANT = {n/k} on
  (1/(n+1), 1/n].  Hence  M f_k(s) = (1/s) sum_n {n/k} [ n^-s - (n+1)^-s ].
  k=2  s=(0.7 + 3.0j)
    direct step-sum          = (0.111110133005 - 0.142911896545j)
    (1/k - k^-s) zeta(s)/s   = (0.111110133062 - 0.142911896438j)   |diff|=1.22e-10
    -k^(s-1) zeta(s)/s       = (-0.127819956588 - 0.0833145108419j)   |diff|=0.246
  k=3  s=(0.6 + 11.0j)
    direct step-sum          = (-0.0262667704767 + 0.024384594596j)
    (1/k - k^-s) zeta(s)/s   = (-0.0262667699775 + 0.0243845951328j)   |diff|=7.33e-10
    -k^(s-1) zeta(s)/s       = (0.0581602004952 + 0.0625894902018j)   |diff|=0.0927
  k=5  s=(0.9 + 1.0j)
    direct step-sum          = (0.11226530804 - 0.213438951951j)
    (1/k - k^-s) zeta(s)/s   = (0.11226530804 - 0.213438951951j)   |diff|=1.82e-16
    -k^(s-1) zeta(s)/s       = (-0.619898849859 + 0.205647667021j)   |diff|=0.844

  Annihilation at the first zeta zero rho1 = 1/2 + 14.134725...i :
    k=2:  |M f_k(rho1)| = 2.86541e-42
    k=3:  |M f_k(rho1)| = 2.19049e-42
    k=7:  |M f_k(rho1)| = 1.18483e-42
  DQ: annihilation is by the COMMON factor zeta(s)/s; the k-dependent factor is a
      Dirichlet polynomial and is generically non-zero.  Nothing here is a proof claim.

