==============================================================================
  principal (1,1,6):  |disc|=23  area constant 2pi/sqrt|D| = 1.3101347027
     total lattice points <= Y : 2620260   main term 2620269   ratio 0.99999641
     sup_{1e3<=y<=2e6} |A(y) - c y| / y^0.333  = 2.2451
     sup_{1e3<=y<=2e6} |A(y) - c y| / y^0.400  = 1.2754
     sup_{1e3<=y<=2e6} |A(y) - c y| / y^0.500  = 0.5461
     k=2: sup |(1/k)A(u) - A(u/k)| / u^(1/3), 1e3<=u<=Y  = 1.4246   ; /u^(1/2) = 0.3784   (bounded ==> Psi^(1) in L^2)
     k=3: sup |(1/k)A(u) - A(u/k)| / u^(1/3), 1e3<=u<=Y  = 1.4296   ; /u^(1/2) = 0.4116   (bounded ==> Psi^(1) in L^2)

  non-principal (2,1,3):  |disc|=23  area constant 2pi/sqrt|D| = 1.3101347027
     total lattice points <= Y : 2620304   main term 2620269   ratio 1.00001320
     sup_{1e3<=y<=2e6} |A(y) - c y| / y^0.333  = 1.9350
     sup_{1e3<=y<=2e6} |A(y) - c y| / y^0.400  = 1.0496
     sup_{1e3<=y<=2e6} |A(y) - c y| / y^0.500  = 0.4842
     k=2: sup |(1/k)A(u) - A(u/k)| / u^(1/3), 1e3<=u<=Y  = 0.8695   ; /u^(1/2) = 0.2444   (bounded ==> Psi^(1) in L^2)
     k=3: sup |(1/k)A(u) - A(u/k)| / u^(1/3), 1e3<=u<=Y  = 0.9983   ; /u^(1/2) = 0.2383   (bounded ==> Psi^(1) in L^2)

  DQ-SECTION
   * A/B blocks: mpmath dps=40; step-sums truncated at N=2e5 with the periodic mean
     removed first, so the tail is O(N^{-sigma-1}) by Abel summation, not O(N^{-sigma}).
   * B3 uses zero coordinates AS QUOTED in our own cycle-11 letter from Math. Comp. 76
     (2007) 2045-2049; |f| there is limited by the printed precision of those digits,
     NOT by the evaluator.  It is a consistency check, not a zero certification.
   * C block: float64 lattice counts, exact integer arithmetic for the counts themselves.
     The exponent lines are an EMPIRICAL check that the classical van der Corput bound
     O(y^{1/3}) is consistent with the data on this range; they do not prove it.
   * No claim in this file is a proof claim, and none of it bears on RH.
